  "term": "portal-systemic encephalopathy",
  "definition": "Portal-systemic encephalopathy is a syndrome of brain dysfunction linked to liver failure, including cases involving portal-systemic shunting. It can cause drowsiness and confusion that may worsen to coma, along with abnormal reflexes and other neurological signs.",
